(*!
<summary>
Beckhoff bidirectional pulse train channel process image.
</summary>
<description>
Combines EL2521 Standard 32-bit (MDP 253/511) input and output endpoints.
Select TxPDOs 0x1A01/0x1A05 and RxPDOs 0x1601/0x1607/0x1605 in enhanced operating mode.
Includes a 16-bit frequency command, 32-bit target, counter feedback and counter preset.
Link input and output fields individually; the aggregate is not one contiguous EtherCAT packet.
Use one owner task; synchronize external access. Copying stores data without creating new hardware links.
When used for I/O, link located fields or their containing buffers to the matching selected PDOs.
The record is not a packed wire buffer; compiler padding is not part of the device specification.
Unlinked/default values do not prove valid I/O. The caller evaluates bus/channel validity before use.
Use one owner task per instance and externally synchronize other access; multi-field snapshots are not atomic.
Copies store data without creating hardware links. Keep borrowed field references valid while consumers are bound.
This passive record performs no validation, synchronization, configuration or protocol advancement.
</description>
*)
TYPE PULSE_TRAIN_CHANNEL :
STRUCT
	In : PULSE_TRAIN_INPUT_CHANNEL;
	Out : PULSE_TRAIN_OUTPUT_CHANNEL;
END_STRUCT
END_TYPE]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>
